# Project structure & build lock

Client-side Vite + React SPA. Live site: `https://daemon-demons.github.io/performance-rag/`.

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `main` | **Source only** — app code, `public/`, workflows. Never commit built `dist/` here. |
| `gh-pages` | **Generated site only** — CI publishes `dist/` here. Never hand-edit. |

## Locked layout (`main`)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `index.html` | Sole Vite entry (`/src/main.jsx`). |
| `src/` | App code (`components/`, `context/`, `pages/`, `utils/`). |
| `public/` | Static files copied into `dist` (sample CSV, favicon, `.nojekyll`). |
| `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` | Sole deploy path: verify → publish `dist` to `gh-pages`. |

Do not invent parallel entrypoints, alternate routers (keep `HashRouter`), or a second deploy workflow unless the user asks.

## Pages / Vite invariants

- Keep `vite.config.js` `base: '/performance-rag/'`.
- Production HTML must reference `/performance-rag/assets/...` — never `/src/main.jsx`.
- GitHub Pages settings: **Deploy from a branch** → `gh-pages` / `/ (root)`.
- Do not publish builds onto `main` (no root `assets/`, no `docs/` site mirror).

## Build must stay green

Before finishing feature work that touches logic, schema, or tooling:

1. `npm test`
2. `npm run lint`
3. `npm run build` (`dist/index.html` must not contain `main.jsx`)

CI on `main` runs the same gates; **deploy runs only after verify passes**.

## CSV / sample schema

Roster columns live in `src/utils/csvSchema.js` (`Is_Departed` optional on upload, always written on save). Sample people: only `scripts/generateSampleRoster.mjs` — run `npm run generate:sample` to refresh `public/sample/`, `sample/`, and `src/utils/sampleCsv.generated.js`.

## Git

Follow `no-auto-push.mdc`: commit/push only when the user explicitly asks.
